2026-09-27T10:19:13.7435986Z Description:
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7436160Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7436319Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7436680Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7437111Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7437154Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7437251Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7437399Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7437545Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7437590Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7437690Z ================
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7437750Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7437827Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7438004Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7438109Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7438165Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7438300Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7438386Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7438454Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7438639Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7438813Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7439129Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7439384Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7439439Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7439653Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7439920Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7440055Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7440199Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7440616Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7440679Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7440814Z ========
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7440891Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7441796Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7442742Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7442923Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7443268Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7443970Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7444424Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7444846Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7445176Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7445519Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7445606Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7495605Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7495759Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7496658Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7497690Z 
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7498230Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7498924Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:19:13.7499082Z 
